From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dirk Fortmeier <d.fortmeier@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:58:02 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Present drawables only after the present wait semaphores
 signal

MVKPresentableSwapchainImage::presentCAMetalDrawable() called
[CAMetalDrawable present] from a scheduled-handler of the present
MTLCommandBuffer. That handler can run before earlier work has finished,
and Metal only defers displaying a drawable for pending render passes
that target it. When the last write to a swapchain image comes from a
compute dispatch or a transfer, the image was displayed before that work
had finished.

Present from the completed-handler of the present MTLCommandBuffer
instead. With semaphores that encode MTLEvent waits, its completion follows
their signals. With the single-queue semaphore style the encoded wait is a
no-op, and ordering relies on command buffers completing in queue order:
observed in 0 of 40 samples out of order, but no Metal document found
guarantees it.

Adopted from https://github.com/fortmeier/MoltenVK/pull/1 (commit
a58d6bcf04ac4a8c1f59652b340411dde760b33a), for
https://github.com/KhronosGroup/MoltenVK/issues/2588.

Modifications:
- An app that destroys the swapchain without waiting (invalid, but seen
  in practice) could crash in beginPresentation() from the handler, which
  now runs later. The base crashes there too in the local probe.
  _swapchain and _device are now read under _detachmentLock there, as
  endPresentation() already does. The rest of the handler is unchanged.
- The comment is corrected for the single-queue semaphore style and a
  modification notice added.
- The Docs/Whats_New.md hunk is dropped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKImage.mm | 22 ++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKImage.mm b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKImage.mm
index 2b394922..b3bbe3b3 100644
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKImage.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKImage.mm
@@ -1650,13 +1650,19 @@ static void signalAndUntrack(const MVKSwapchainSignaler& signaler) {
 															  MVKImagePresentInfo presentInfo) {
 	_swapchain->renderWatermark(getMTLTexture(0), mtlCmdBuff);
 
-	// According to Apple, it is more performant to call MTLDrawable present from within a
-	// MTLCommandBuffer scheduled-handler than it is to call MTLCommandBuffer presentDrawable:.
-	// But get current drawable now, intead of in handler, because a new drawable might be acquired by then.
+	// Downstream change (not in upstream MoltenVK): completed-handler instead of scheduled-handler.
+	// Present from a MTLCommandBuffer completed-handler. With semaphores that encode MTLEvent waits, the
+	// present MTLCommandBuffer holds those waits, so its completion follows their signals. With the
+	// single-queue semaphore style the encoded wait is a no-op, and ordering relies on command buffers
+	// completing in queue order, which was observed but which no Metal document guarantees. A
+	// scheduled-handler, or MTLCommandBuffer presentDrawable:, can run before the earlier work finishes,
+	// and Metal only defers the display of a drawable for pending render passes that target it. Content
+	// written to the drawable by compute or transfer commands would then be displayed too early.
+	// Get current drawable now, intead of in handler, because a new drawable might be acquired by then.
 	// Attach present handler before presenting to avoid race condition.
 	id<CAMetalDrawable> mtlDrwbl = getCAMetalDrawable();
 	MVKSwapchainSignaler signaler = getPresentationSignaler();
-	[mtlCmdBuff addScheduledHandler: ^(id<MTLCommandBuffer> mcb) {
+	[mtlCmdBuff addCompletedHandler: ^(id<MTLCommandBuffer> mcb) {
 
 		addPresentedHandler(mtlDrwbl, presentInfo, signaler);
 
@@ -1737,9 +1743,13 @@ static void signalAndUntrack(const MVKSwapchainSignaler& signaler) {
 // Ensure this image and the swapchain are not destroyed while awaiting presentation
 void MVKPresentableSwapchainImage::beginPresentation(const MVKImagePresentInfo& presentInfo) {
 	retain();
-	_swapchain->beginPresentation(presentInfo);
+	{	// Downstream change (not in upstream MoltenVK): this now runs from a completed-handler,
+		// which an app that destroys the swapchain without waiting can outrun.
+		lock_guard<mutex> lock(_detachmentLock);
+		if (_swapchain) { _swapchain->beginPresentation(presentInfo); }
+		if (_device) { _presentationStartTime = getPerformanceTimestamp(); }
+	}
 	_beginPresentTime = mvkGetRuntimeNanoseconds();
-	_presentationStartTime = getPerformanceTimestamp();
 }
 
 void MVKPresentableSwapchainImage::endPresentation(const MVKImagePresentInfo& presentInfo,
